# Twisted Roots Merc — HTTP response headers
#
# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ MOVE THIS FILE TO THE REPO ROOT.  It must live at ./_headers (next to    │
# │ index.html), with no file extension. It does nothing inside deploy/.     │
# │   Cloudflare Pages: reads ./_headers. Netlify: reads ./_headers too.     │
# │   GitHub Pages: IGNORES THIS FILE ENTIRELY — GH Pages cannot set custom  │
# │   headers at all. That is one of the reasons it is not recommended.      │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# Syntax: a path pattern on its own line, then indented "Name: value" lines.
# `*` is a wildcard. Verify a change took effect with:
#   curl -sSI https://twistedrootsmerc.com/ | sort
#   curl -sSI https://twistedrootsmerc.com/assets/css/site.css | sort
#
# Deliberately NO Cache-Control in the /* block — Cache-Control is set per
# path below so two matching rules can never fight over the same header name.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECURITY — every response
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(self), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# ── Why each CSP directive is what it is (read before you "tighten" it) ────
#
# script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
#     REQUIRED, and it is the weakest part of this policy. Two things need it:
#       1. index.html has <script type="application/ld+json"> (the
#          LocalBusiness schema Google reads). Yes — CSP treats ld+json as an
#          inline script and blocks it without 'unsafe-inline'. Blocked, you
#          silently lose your rich result in Google.
#       2. hq.html has a ~110-line inline <script> block (line 188) that
#          builds the reorder table.
#     'unsafe-inline' means CSP is NOT protecting you from script injection.
#     Mitigating fact, verified in this codebase: every value interpolated
#     into .innerHTML in assets/js/site.js goes through the esc() helper
#     (site.js:34), including the search query read from ?q=. So there is no
#     known injection point today — but CSP is no longer your safety net, so
#     keep it that way.
#
#     TO GO NONCE-BASED (real hardening, needs page edits — another agent
#     owns the HTML, so this is a request, not something done here):
#       a. Move hq.html's inline <script> into assets/js/hq.js.
#       b. Move index.html's ld+json into a static /schema.jsonld file
#          referenced by <script type="application/ld+json" src="...">  —
#          NOTE: Google does NOT reliably read src'd ld+json. The realistic
#          alternative is to keep the ld+json inline and give it a nonce.
#       c. Nonces must be regenerated per request, which a static file cannot
#          do. On Cloudflare Pages that means a Pages Function that rewrites
#          the HTML on the fly. For a ten-page store site that is a lot of
#          moving parts for a small win. Recommendation: do (a), which at
#          least removes the hq.html block, and keep 'unsafe-inline' for the
#          one ld+json island. Revisit only if the site ever accepts and
#          re-displays untrusted input.
#
# style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com
#     'unsafe-inline' is REQUIRED: the pages carry ~150 inline style=""
#     attributes (12–21 per page), and CSP blocks those without it. There are
#     no <style> blocks. fonts.googleapis.com serves the Bitter / Public Sans
#     / Rye stylesheet linked in every <head>.
#     Removing 'unsafe-inline' here means moving every style="" attribute into
#     site.css. Doable, ~150 edits, low value — style injection is a far
#     smaller risk than script injection.
#
# font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com
#     The Google Fonts stylesheet pulls the actual .woff2 files from gstatic.
#     Miss this and the fonts silently fall back to system serif/sans.
#
# img-src 'self' data:
#     data: is not used today (checked) but costs nothing and keeps future
#     inline SVG/placeholder work from breaking.
#
# media-src 'self'
#     assets/video/*.mp4 — the hero, storm, rain and woodgrain background
#     clips. Note Permissions-Policy above allows autoplay=(self) for these.
#
# connect-src 'self'
#     The site makes ZERO network calls today (no fetch/XHR anywhere in
#     assets/js/). WHEN THE SQUARE SYNC LANDS: put the endpoint on the SAME
#     origin (a Pages Function at /api/catalog) and this line keeps working
#     untouched. If instead you call a separate *.workers.dev host, you must
#     add it here or the browser blocks the request with a console error that
#     looks nothing like a CSP problem.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options: DENY
#     Same intent, two generations of browser. Nobody can iframe the store.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CACHING — long and immutable for media, short for versionless CSS/JS
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# THE TRADEOFF, stated plainly. Nothing in assets/ has a content hash in its
# filename (site.css, not site.a1b2c3.css) because there is no build step. So:
#
#   • Images and video CAN be cached for a year, because the convention here
#     is that a photo is replaced by ADDING a new filename, not by overwriting
#     one. If you ever overwrite assets/img/hero-store.jpg in place, visitors
#     who have been to the site keep the old photo for up to a year and there
#     is nothing you can do about it. RULE: never overwrite an image; add
#     hero-store-2.jpg and point the page at it.
#
#   • CSS and JS CANNOT safely be cached for a year, because site.css and
#     site.js DO get edited in place — that is the whole workflow. They get
#     max-age=300 + must-revalidate: after 5 minutes the browser asks "changed?"
#     and gets a 4-byte 304 if not. Cost: one tiny conditional request per
#     file per 5 minutes per visitor. Benefit: a CSS fix is live for everyone
#     within 5 minutes, every time, with no cache-busting discipline required.
#     For a ten-page site with fewer visitors than a coffee shop has
#     customers, this is the right trade. Do not "optimise" it.
#
#   • IF you later want year-long CSS/JS caching, the cache-busting approach
#     that works without a build step is a query string in the HTML:
#         <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/site.css?v=7">
#         <script src="assets/js/site.js?v=7"></script>
#     bump v on every edit, then change the /assets/css/* and /assets/js/*
#     rules below to `max-age=31536000, immutable`. THE TRADEOFF: it only
#     works if someone remembers to bump the number. Forget once and you ship
#     a change that you can see (your browser revalidated) and customers
#     cannot, for a year, with no error anywhere. That failure mode is nasty
#     enough that it is not worth it here. Only adopt it if a real build step
#     arrives and does the bumping automatically.

/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/video/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HTML — always revalidate, so a copy fix is live immediately
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Both spellings of every page are listed. Cloudflare Pages 308-redirects
# /merc.html to /merc, so /merc is the path that actually gets served — but
# the .html form is listed too so the rules still hold if you ever move hosts
# or the redirect behaviour changes. See DEPLOY.md → "The one big gotcha".

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/merc
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/merc.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/bakery
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/bakery.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/yard
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/yard.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/storm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/storm.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/local
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/local.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/board
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/board.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/roots
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/roots.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/visit
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/visit.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/404
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/404.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# robots.txt and sitemap.xml: short cache so a fix propagates to crawlers.
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE PRIVATE OWNER DASHBOARD
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# These headers are hygiene, NOT protection. They keep the page out of search
# results and out of caches. They do not stop a single person from opening it.
# Real protection is Cloudflare Access — see DEPLOY.md section 4.

/hq
  Cache-Control: private, no-store, max-age=0
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet
/hq.html
  Cache-Control: private, no-store, max-age=0
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet
